class Solution {
    public String longestCommonPrefix(String[] strs) {
        Arrays.sort(strs);
        String s1 = strs[0];
        String s2 = strs[strs.length-1];
        int idx = 0;
        while(idx < s1.length() && idx < s2.length()){
            if(s1.charAt(idx) == s2.charAt(idx)){
                idx++;
            } else {
                break;
            }
        }
        return s1.substring(0, idx);
    }
}

#complexity note:
## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** O(n × m)
- **Space Complexity:** O(1)

### Explanation
- `n` = number of strings.
- `m` = length of the shortest string.
- We compare characters across the strings until a mismatch is found.
- No extra data structure is used, so the extra space is **O(1)**.
